p;cat&#x3d;2&amp;id&#x3d;0701D22C&amp;sort&#x3d;8&amp;cid&#x3d;2013&amp;sid&#x3d;1\" title=\"DTN&#x20;Closing&#x20;Livestock&#x20;Comment&#x20;10&#x2f;14&#x20;15&#x3a;37&#x20;\">8</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"&#x3f;show&#x3d;801&amp;cat&#x3d;2&amp;id&#x3d;0700B8D9&amp;sort&#x3d;9&amp;cid&#x3d;2013&amp;sid&#x3d;1\" title=\"DTN&#x20;Chart&#x20;Technical&#x20;Points&#x20;&#x20;&#x20;&#x20;&#x20;&#x20;&#x20;&#x20;&#x20;&#x20;&#x20;&#x20;&#x20;10&#x2f;16&#x20;16&#x3a;30&#x20;\">9</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"&#x3f;show&#x3d;801&amp;cat&#x3d;2&amp;id&#x3d;0700B8F3&amp;sort&#x3d;10&amp;cid&#x3d;2013&amp;sid&#x3d;1\" title=\"National&#x20;Lean&#x20;Hog&#x20;Values&#x20;\">10</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</font>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</tr>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t</table>\n\t\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t\t<td width=\"2%\">&nbsp;</td>\n\t\t\t\t</tr>\n\t\t\n\t<tr> \n\t\t<td width=\"2%\">&nbsp;</td>\n\t\t<td colspan=\"2\">\n\t\t\t<pre style=\"font-size:14px; font-family: courier\">\r\nDTN Midday Grain Comments     10/14 10:48\r\n\r\n   Midday Wednesday: Corn, Soybeans and Wheat All Lower\r\n\r\n   Corn futures are 4 to 5 cents lower at midday, soybeans are 9 to 11 cents \r\nlower, and wheat futures are 5 to 8 cents lower. \r\n\r\nDavid M. Fiala\r\nDTN Contributing Analyst\r\n\r\nMARKET SUMMARY:\r\n\r\n   Corn futures are 4 to 5 cents lower at midday, soybeans are 9 to 11 cents \r\nlower, and wheat futures are 5 to 8 cents lower. The U.S. stock market is \r\nweaker at midday with the S&P 65 points lower. The dollar index is 72 points \r\nhigher. The interest rate products are weaker. Energy trade is mixed with crude \r\n.70 higher and natural gas .08 cents lower. Livestock trade is broadly weaker. \r\nPrecious metals are sharply lower with gold off 65.\r\n\r\nCORN:\r\n\r\n   Corn futures are 4 to 5 cents lower at midday with trade drifting along the \r\nrecent range with harvest continuing to catch up short term with the post \r\nreport lows still holding. Ethanol margins remain strong short term with the \r\nweekly report delayed until tomorrow.\r\n\r\n   The daily export wire was quiet Wednesday. Weather looks to slow some \r\nwestern and central harvest through midweek as rains return with the weekly \r\nreport showing harvest at 33% vs. 39% on average with good to excellent at \r\n56%(+2) and poor to very poor at 17%(-1). Basis will likely see a bit of \r\npressure as harvest continues. On the December chart the 20-day at $5.10 is \r\nresistance with the fresh low at $4.70 1/4 being support.\r\n\r\nSOYBEANS:\r\n\r\n   Soybeans are 9 to 11 cents lower at midday with trade washing back towards \r\nthe lows after early strength with harvest pressure and negative outside \r\nmarkets. Meal is 4 to 5 lower and oil is 90 to 100 points lower. Harvest maybe \r\nslowed a bit with short-term rains in the central and west expected with the \r\nweekly report showing 46% harvested vs. 50% on average with good to excellent \r\nsteady at 57% good to excellent and 14% poor to very poor. The daily export \r\nwire was quiet again. Basis should see maximum harvest pressure soon. On the \r\nNovember contract chart resistance is the 20-day at 12.97 where we find the \r\n20-day moving average with the Lower Bollinger Band at 12.71 which we bounced \r\nfrom Friday.\r\n\r\nWHEAT:\r\n\r\n   Wheat futures are 5 to 8 cents lower at midday with choppy action continuing \r\nas the dollar firms back towards recent highs and row crops continue to drag a \r\nlittle on action. Drier weather should help wheat drilling catch up for much of \r\nthe Plains 51% planted vs. 58% on average with 27% emerged vs. 32% on average. \r\nMatif wheat is firmer with Euro corn continuing to gain as well with extra \r\nsupport from the weaker Euro/Stronger dollar. On the KC December chart \r\nresistance is the 20-day at $7.48 with the fresh low at $7.05 as support.\r\n\r\n   David Fiala can be reached at dfiala@futuresone.com\r\n\r\n   Follow him on social platform X @davidfiala\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n(c) Copyright 2026 DTN, LLC. All rights reserved.\r\n\r\n</pre> \n\t<div style=\"text-align:center; border:1px solid #cccccc; background-color:#ffffff;color:#000000;padding:5px;margin:5px;font-size:8pt;font-family:arial, helvetica neue, helvetica, sans-serif,sans-serif;\">\n\t\tNo other Daily email offers as much useful Ag information as DTN Snapshot &ndash; <a style=\"color:#666666\" href=\"http://agnews.dtn.com/pivot.cfm?id=82&mkt=0\" target=\"_blank\">Sign up</a> Free today!\n\t</div>\n\n\t\t</td>\n\t\t<td width=\"2%\">&nbsp;</td>\n\t</tr>\n</table>\n\n</td></tr></table>\n\n<div align=\"center\">\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"800\">\n\t<tr><td height=\"10\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\n\t<tr><td bgcolor=\"ffffff\" align=\"center\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica neue, helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"1\" color=\"000000\">Copyright DTN.  All rights reserved.  <a href=\"https://www.aghost.net/disclaimer.cfm\" target=\"disclaimer\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica neue, helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"1\" color=\"000000\">Disclaimer</font></a>.</font></td></tr>\n    \n\t<tr><td align=\"center\"><a href=\"https&#x3a;&#x2f;&#x2f;www.dtnpf.com&#x2f;agriculture&#x2f;web&#x2f;ag&#x2f;home\" rel=\"nofollow\"><img src=\"/images/alpha/dtnpf_bw_120x42.png?show&#x3d;801&amp;mid&#x3d;-1&amp;cat&#x3d;2&amp;IFRAME&#x3d;false&amp;sort&#x3d;3&amp;id&#x3d;0701D229&amp;ShowMenu&#x3d;1\" width=\"120\" height=\"42\" border=\"0\" alt=\"Powered By DTN\"></a>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n</div>\n\n</body>\n</html>\n"
 },
